# Omni-Changeling: the exception "it has changeling" is part of the copy's own copiable values (CR 707.9b), so a later copy of it has
# changeling as well, though the Ornithopter it copied has none. Turn 1: Omni-Changeling convokes three Ornithopters and enters as a copy of
# one (the fourth Ornithopter). Turn 3: Phantasmal Image enters as a copy of that fourth Ornithopter, an Illusion in addition to its other
# types, with changeling and the Image's own sacrifice ability: it is every creature type (a plain third Ornithopter is only a Thopter).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Omni-Changeling
Phantasmal Image
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Omni-Changeling.Cast(Convoke: Ornithopter, Ornithopter, Ornithopter)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Phantasmal Image.Cast
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#4)
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#5.Keywords = Changeling; Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#5.Subtypes = (every creature type)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Subtypes = Thopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Subtypes = (every creature type)
